From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tonrakun <tonrakun@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:34:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Kodama: adapt chunk loading to player behaviour

License: GPL-3.0

Classifies every player as settler, commuter or explorer from the five
minute window of PlayerMotion (new chunks per minute, speed, elytra and
vehicle share, range). A type only switches after it won for
type-switch-seconds. The type and moving averages of new chunks and speed
are stored in the player data (tag Kodama) and give the starting value of
the next session.

Settlers get no prefetch and settler-unload-delay-seconds. Commuters get
the remembered route chunks ahead of them prefetched first, from a ring
buffer of the last route-memory-chunks positions. Explorers get the
prefetch distance and angle multiplied by explorer-prefetch-multiplier,
and the precache takes its explorers from the classifier. An optional
server-wide budget (budget-chunks-per-second minus min-per-player for each
online player) limits prefetch and pre-generation and prefers explorers.

Controlled by chunk-loading.adaptive.*; with the switch off the chunk
loading behaves as before. /kodama status lists type, new chunks per
minute and speed per player and the budget.

